        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> What's the downside of triggering the callback on keymaps? Can it result in an autocompletando being selected?\n\nThe obvious issue is performance: `CmdlineEnter` and `CmdlineLeave` are triggered once, `CmdlineChanged` is triggered after every character change inside a mapping. I'd want to avoid having this if possible, as autocommand callback (which opens/closes floating window, for example) has no business being triggered on a regular mapping.\n\nThe other issue of dropping `vim.schedule_wrap(H.on_cmdline_enter)` in favor of `H.on_cmdline_enter` is the (correctly) failing test. It tests that hiding visual selection can be disabled by a properly documented set of autocommands, and the fail shows that autocommands do not work. That approach requires checking command line content which is empty on the plain `CmdlineEnter` and is populated if scheduled. Which has problems cooperating with non-scheduled `H.on_cmdline_enter`.\n\nIt is tricky.",
